  "rationale": "Thelonious Monk's first Riverside album built entirely from his own compositions, routinely cited as the definitive studio statement of his 1950s comeback. It pairs Monk with a peerless hard-bop cohort—Sonny Rollins, Max Roach, Clark Terry, Ernie Henry, Oscar Pettiford, and Paul Chambers—and was named by DownBeat the most acclaimed jazz LP of 1957. Penguin Guide lists it in the core collection; the title track's editing-from-multiple-takes legend only adds to its canonical weight. Strong consensus + defining statement + session gravity.",
